<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Borwin II, Lord of Mecklenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1170–1226</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Borwin II was a lord of Mecklenburg of the native Obotrite dynasty, ruling jointly with his father Henry Borwin I in the early 13th century, when German settlers and new towns transformed the region. He died in 1226, before his father, and in 1229 his lands were divided among his four sons, creating the lordships of Mecklenburg, Werle, Rostock and Parchim-Richenberg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-borwin-ii-lord-of-mecklenburg.jpg" alt="Henry Borwin II, Lord of Mecklenburg" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Norbert Kaiser · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%BCstrow_Borwin-Brunnen_Heinrich_Borwin_II_F%C3%BCrst_zu_Mecklenburg_(01-2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
